10	--
11	### What happened?
12	
13	Preamble: I'm not certain of this issue, but empirically it exists with `entire enable` and it goes away with `entire disable`
14	
15	System info:
16	Mac OS Tahoe 26.2
17	zsh
18	ghostty 1.3.1
19	opencode 1.3.17
20	Entire CLI 0.5.5 (90bb1c50)
21	Go version: go1.26.2
22	OS/Arch: darwin/arm64
23	
24	Issue:
25	
26	When I use `opencode` with `entire` enabled, I encountered the following two issues which significantly impacted my development experience:
27	- The "escape twice to interrupt" feature is much less reliable, often not working at all. I use this feature frequently
28	- The "step end" sequence to finalize an agent response often hangs. The "loader / racing squares" (denoting that the agent is working) continue racing despite the agent producing the finalized summary response
29	
30	### Steps to reproduce
31	
32	1. entire enable
33	2. opencode
34	3. prompt any action with the  "build" agent. note that this is an occasionally reproducible bug, so not a consistent set of steps
35	
36	### Entire CLI version
